  "validationRule": "Every listed path must exist and match SHA-256 exactly. The artifact list is unique and the manifest excludes only itself. R1 through R9 critic records are immutable correction inputs. Every declared fixture/vector ID and coverage kind must execute through the shared schema or semantic oracle with exact state, first error, and typed effects. R3 through R8 closures remain executable. R9 requires an immutable registry digest and independently selected provider binding in the manifest and signed lifecycle context. Verification selects the sole valid non-revoked public key, algorithm, provider/account/tenant scope, proof type, and issuer from that binding, never from receipt self-claims, while provider-only fixture private keys remain separate from sealRecord. Distinct-provider and rotation-boundary positives pass; local-signer forgery, relabel, cross-provider, unknown/revoked/expired/future key, wrong algorithm/issuer/account/tenant, registry mismatch, proof/preimage tamper, and duplicate transaction deny with typed zero effects. Exact committed same-byte replay remains effect-free. This unsigned R9-corrected candidate awaits a fresh-context safety/completeness preflight before authorized GitHub App incorporation; non-canonical status alone is not a pre-incorporation defect."
